<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madura</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madura is an island off the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> province, separated from Java by the narrow Madura Strait. Drier and less fertile than Java, it is known for salt production, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> raising and bull races, and its people, the Madurese, speak their own language. Madura was contested by Javanese kingdoms, conquered by Mataram in 1624 and later ruled by Dutch-backed regents.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madura.jpg" alt="Madura" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Nurfikr08 at Indonesian Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Labhang_Mesem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
